IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-admin-sin`

-- Tests of er5-admin-sin (reg 89). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1678-1683),
-- beside each assertion, before the run. "Within three days after the day on which the employment begins" ends on that day plus three, and that day counts.

§ `Reg 89(1) - applying to be registered (src:1678)`

-- The argument order is: employed in insurable employment; required by section 138 to have a number; has not yet applied to be registered.
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Already applied: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The employment begins on March 2, 2020; three days after is March 5, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` (YMD 2020 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 5
-- Across a month end in a leap year: February 27, 2020 plus three days is March 1, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` (YMD 2020 2 27) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
-- And in a year that is not a leap year: February 26, 2021 plus three days is March 1, 2021.
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` (YMD 2021 2 26) EQUALS YMD 2021 3 1
-- Applying on the last day is in time; the day after is not; before the employment began is in time.
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the person applies to be registered within three days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(1) the person applies to be registered within three days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 6))
#ASSERT `reg 89(1) the person applies to be registered within three days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 2 20)

§ `Reg 89(2) - the employer asks the employee (src:1679)`

#ASSERT `reg 89(2) the employer must ask the employee to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(2) the employer must ask the employee to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 89(2) the last day on which the employer must ask the employee` (YMD 2020 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 5
#ASSERT `reg 89(2) the employer asks the employee within three days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(2) the employer asks the employee within three days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 6))

§ `Reg 89(3) and (4) - the person informs the employer (src:1680-1681)`

-- The argument order of the last day is: the day the employment begins; employed before being registered; the day the number is received, if it has been.
-- A person registered when the employment begins on March 2, 2020: three days after the employment begins.
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` (YMD 2020 3 2) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)
-- The same person, though a number was received on March 20, 2020: (4) does not apply, so (3) still governs.
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` (YMD 2020 3 2) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 20)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)
-- Employed before being registered, number received on March 20, 2020: three days after receipt.
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` (YMD 2020 3 2) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 20)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 3 23)
-- Employed before being registered and no number received yet: no time is running.
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` (YMD 2020 3 2) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Informing in time: on the last day, a day late, never, and when no time is running.
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 6)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 3 6))

§ `Reg 89(5) - the employer reports (src:1682)`

#ASSERT `reg 89(5) the employer must report the matter to the local office of the Commission` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(5) the employer must report the matter to the local office of the Commission` FALSE)
-- Six days after March 2, 2020 is March 8, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 89(5) the last day on which the employer must report the matter` (YMD 2020 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 8
#ASSERT `reg 89(5) the employer reports the matter within six days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(5) the employer reports the matter within six days after the day on which the employment begins` (YMD 2020 3 2) (YMD 2020 3 9))

§ `Reg 89(6) - a change in the number or its validity (src:1683)`

-- The argument order is: employed in insurable employment; validity extended; a new period of validity assigned; a new number assigned.
#ASSERT `reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- No change at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not employed in insurable employment.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Informed of the change on March 10, 2020: three days after is March 13, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 89(6) the last day on which the person must inform their employer of the change` (YMD 2020 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 13
#ASSERT `reg 89(6) the person informs their employer of the change within three days after the day they are informed of it` (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2020 3 13)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 89(6) the person informs their employer of the change within three days after the day they are informed of it` (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2020 3 14))
